faqs:
  - q: How is this different from dedicated squads?
    a: Scale and horizon. Squads are 3 to 7 people committed by the quarter. ODCs are 8 to 50 people committed by the year. Long-tenured engineers, not rotating ones.
  - q: Do we interview the team?
    a: Yes. Every engineer is interviewed by your team before placement. Replacement at our cost if someone does not fit within the first month.
  - q: Where do the engineers sit?
    a: India, Poland, Mexico, Brazil, or Vietnam. Chosen for the skill mix and cost target. We run delivery presence in each location, not contract arrangements.
  - q: Who owns the code?
    a: You do. Code pushed to your repos. Environments in your accounts. No vendor lock-in.
  - q: How do you handle attrition?
    a: Dedicated engineers sign on for a minimum term. Attrition tracked as a program metric. Replacement process rehearsed so it is not a scramble when someone leaves.
